    "body": "Fixes #7824\r\n\r\nThis handles Python strings, or things that get added to the stringtab. It can't (easily) handle a lot of other places, like docstrings, where the string literal is just passed directly. This seems to account for almost all uses of `as_c_string_literal` so I've just disallowed generating the array definition from that. The other case that it can't easily handle is `BytesNodes.generate_evaluation_code`\r\n\r\n```\r\n            # not const => use plain C string literal and cast to mutable type\r\n            literal = self.value.as_c_string_literal()\r\n            # C++ may require a cast\r\n            result = typecast(self.type, PyrexTypes.c_void_ptr_type, literal)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI've made it conditional on MSVC. Compiling these array definitions is hugely slow on GCC (I got bored waiting for it to finish so I don't actually know how long...).",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-17T08:15:36Z",
