                    "name": "da-woods"
                },
                "message": "Handle long C strings in MSVC\n\nFixes #7824\n\nThis handles Python strings, or things that get added to the\nstringtab. It can't (easily) handle a lot of other places, like\ndocstrings, where the string literal is just passed directly.\nThis seems to account for almost all uses of `as_c_string_literal`\nso I've just disallowed generating the array definition from that.\nThe other case that it can't easily handle is `BytesNodes.generate_evaluation_code`\n\n```\n            # not const => use plain C string literal and cast to mutable type\n            literal = self.value.as_c_string_literal()\n            # C++ may require a cast\n            result = typecast(self.type, PyrexTypes.c_void_ptr_type, literal)\n```\n\nI've made it conditional on MSVC. Compiling these array\ndefinitions is hugely slow on GCC (I got bored waiting for it\nto finish so I don't actually know how long...).",
